1. DEPENDENCY INJECTION AND INVERSION OF CONTROL
==============================================================================

DEPENDENCY INJECTION:

Dependency Injection means providing an object's dependencies from outside
instead of creating them inside the class.

Without DI:

@Service
public class PaymentService {

    private PaymentRepository repository =
            new PaymentRepository();
}

With DI:

@Service
public class PaymentService {

    private final PaymentRepository repository;

    public PaymentService(PaymentRepository repository) {
        this.repository = repository;
    }
}

INVERSION OF CONTROL:

IoC means Spring controls object creation, configuration, lifecycle, and
dependency management instead of our application code.

Flow:

Spring Container
      |
      +--> Creates PaymentRepository
      |
      +--> Creates PaymentService
      |
      +--> Injects Repository into Service

SHORT DIFFERENCE:

IoC = Overall principle where control is given to Spring.

DI = Technique through which Spring supplies dependencies.

INTERVIEW ANSWER:

"IOC means Spring controls object creation and lifecycle. Dependency Injection
is the mechanism by which Spring supplies required objects to a class,
improving loose coupling and testability."

