4. WHAT DOES map() DO?
==============================================================================

map() transforms every stream element into another value.

Flow:

banana --> BANANA
apple  --> APPLE

Example:

List<Integer> lengths = fruits.stream()
        .map(String::length)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

Output:

[6, 5]

ONE-LINER:

"map performs one-to-one transformation and returns a new stream."

==============================================================================
5. DIFFERENCE BETWEEN filter() AND map()
==============================================================================

filter():

Selects elements based on a condition.

List<String> result = fruits.stream()
        .filter(s -> s.startsWith("a"))
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

Output:

[apple]

map():

Transforms elements.

List<String> result = fruits.stream()
        .map(String::toUpperCase)
        .collect(Collectors.toList());

Output:

[BANANA, APPLE]

SHORT DIFFERENCE:

filter = Select data

map = Transform data

