12. WHAT ARE MICROSERVICES AND WHY KAFKA?
==============================================================================

Microservices architecture divides a large application into small,
independently deployable services organized around business capabilities.

Example:

Payment Service
Risk Service
Audit Service
Notification Service

Why Kafka:

• Asynchronous communication
• Loose coupling
• High event throughput
• Durable event storage
• Replay capability
• Multiple independent consumers
• Partition-based parallel processing

INTERVIEW ANSWER:

"We used microservices to independently develop, deploy, and scale business
capabilities. Kafka was used for high-volume asynchronous events where the
producer should not wait for every downstream consumer."

