13. WHY KAFKA INSTEAD OF REST API?
==============================================================================

REST:

Payment Service
      |
      v
Notification API
      |
Wait for Response

If Notification API is unavailable, the caller may fail or wait.

Kafka:

Payment Service
      |
      v
payment-topic
      |
      +--> Notification Consumer
      |
      +--> Audit Consumer
      |
      +--> Reporting Consumer

Kafka is preferred when:

• Immediate response is not required
• Multiple systems need the same event
• Producer and consumer need loose coupling
• Events must survive temporary consumer downtime
• Replay or high throughput is required

REST is preferred when:

• Immediate response is required
• The requester needs the result before continuing

ONE-LINER:

"REST is synchronous request-response communication; Kafka provides durable,
asynchronous, event-driven communication."

