14. WHAT IS A KAFKA PARTITION?
==============================================================================

A Kafka topic is divided into partitions.

Example:

payment-topic

Partition-0
Partition-1
Partition-2

Benefits:

• Parallel consumer processing
• Horizontal scalability
• Distributed storage
• Ordering within each partition

Messages with the same key are normally routed consistently so related events
can maintain partition-level order.

Example:

paymentId = P1001 --> Partition-1

Kafka topics must have sufficient partitions to support desired consumer
concurrency. 【1-fa3f59】

