16. WHAT IS AN IMMUTABLE SEQUENCE IN A PARTITION?
==============================================================================

Correct Kafka term:

An append-only ordered log.

Events are appended to the end of a partition and assigned sequential offsets.

Example:

Partition-0:

Offset 0 --> Event-A
Offset 1 --> Event-B
Offset 2 --> Event-C

Existing records are not updated like normal database rows.

Important:

Kafka guarantees record ordering within a partition, not across all partitions.

