22. WHAT IS PROTOTYPE SCOPE?
HOW TO CHANGE SINGLETON TO PROTOTYPE?
==============================================================================

Prototype scope creates a new bean instance whenever the bean is requested
from the Spring container. 【2-090452】

Code:

@Component
@Scope(ConfigurableBeanFactory.SCOPE_PROTOTYPE)
public class ReportBuilder {
}

Alternative:

@Component
@Scope("prototype")
public class ReportBuilder {
}

Configuration using @Bean:

@Configuration
public class AppConfig {

    @Bean
    @Scope(ConfigurableBeanFactory.SCOPE_PROTOTYPE)
    public ReportBuilder reportBuilder() {
        return new ReportBuilder();
    }
}

SHORT DIFFERENCE:

Singleton:

One shared bean instance per IoC container.

Prototype:

New instance each time the container is asked for the bean.

IMPORTANT FOLLOW-UP:

Directly constructor-injecting a prototype bean into a singleton usually
resolves the prototype at singleton creation time. When a fresh instance is
required repeatedly, use ObjectProvider.

Code:

@Service
public class ReportService {

    private final ObjectProvider<ReportBuilder> provider;

    public ReportService(
            ObjectProvider<ReportBuilder> provider) {
        this.provider = provider;
    }

    public void generate() {
        ReportBuilder builder = provider.getObject();
    }
}

